
  - [1mBase URL only[0m — settings exposes [38;5;153mapiBaseUrl[39m; [38;5;153mapp.js[39m composes [38;5;153m`${apiBaseUrl}/login`[39m. Buys: adding a second endpoint
    later needs no settings change, and the settings file stays a pure environment table. Costs: endpoint paths are
    scattered across feature code.
  - [1mFull URLs per endpoint[0m — settings exposes [38;5;153mendpoints.login[39m as a complete URL per environment. Buys: one place to see
    every URL. Costs: every new endpoint means editing every environment block — the table grows by environments ×
    endpoints.
  - [1mBase + path map[0m — settings exposes [38;5;153mapiBaseUrl[39m plus a shared [38;5;153mpaths: { login: "/login" }[39m. Buys: both, centralized
    paths without per-environment duplication. Costs: a second concept in a file holding one value.

  I recommend [1mbase URL only[0m. You have exactly one endpoint; the path map is structure bought for a second endpoint that
  doesn't exist yet, and promoting [38;5;153mapiBaseUrl[39m to a base-plus-paths shape later is additive rather than breaking.

